00:46:38.029 --> 00:46:40.396
You fucking said it.


00:46:40.398 --> 00:46:42.265
- Excuse me.
- Oh.


00:46:42.267 --> 00:46:43.666
Well, he still has
my diary then.


00:46:43.668 --> 00:46:44.901
Bravo, Joe.


00:46:44.903 --> 00:46:47.770
- He didn't want my paper.
- Well, he's got taste.


00:47:01.518 --> 00:47:03.085
<i>I don't want to die.</i>


00:47:04.254 --> 00:47:07.056
<i>I want to get married</i>
<i>and have children.</i>


00:47:08.158 --> 00:47:10.118
<i>I want to create</i>
<i>something good.</i>


00:47:11.461 --> 00:47:13.229
<i>I want to get old.</i>


00:47:13.630 --> 00:47:15.598
<i>I want my time.</i>


00:47:15.600 --> 00:47:17.266
<i>I want my life.</i>


00:47:18.869 --> 00:47:21.671
<i>I don't know where</i>
<i>I could have got HIV from.</i>


00:47:32.049 --> 00:47:33.149
Hey.


00:47:33.151 --> 00:47:35.117
Hi, stranger,
long time, no see.


00:47:36.253 --> 00:47:40.056
- I was back in London.
- Nice. What can I get you?


00:47:40.058 --> 00:47:41.791
- Whiskey and coke.
- Cool.


00:47:43.727 --> 00:47:46.295
I was wondering,
could you do me a favor?


00:47:46.297 --> 00:47:47.463
Of course.


00:47:47.465 --> 00:47:49.799
Do you know where
I could buy some stuff?


00:47:49.801 --> 00:47:51.133
What, weed?


00:47:51.135 --> 00:47:53.302
Yeah, but...
But some other stuff too.


00:47:53.304 --> 00:47:55.838
Remember what
happened last time.


00:47:55.840 --> 00:47:58.975
- Thanks, I do.
- Is that what you want?


00:47:58.977 --> 00:48:01.611
- I'm not a dealer.
- I know.


00:48:01.613 --> 00:48:03.880
I just thought you might
be able to help a friend.


00:48:05.315 --> 00:48:06.649
That's better.


00:48:07.718 --> 00:48:09.051
Give me your phone.


00:48:13.690 --> 00:48:16.058
That's the number.
Be careful.


00:48:16.526 --> 00:48:17.593
Promise.


00:48:21.565 --> 00:48:23.132
Hi, it's me, Thomas.


00:48:23.134 --> 00:48:24.333
Are you here?


00:48:24.335 --> 00:48:25.835
<i>I'm here, where are you?</i>


00:48:25.837 --> 00:48:26.969
I'm here.


00:48:26.971 --> 00:48:28.471
Okay, I see you.


00:48:30.007 --> 00:48:32.141
So, you're a friend of Melanie?


00:48:32.143 --> 00:48:33.209
Yeah.


00:48:55.599 --> 00:48:57.767
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:48:57.769 --> 00:48:59.802
- You wanna come in?
- Sure.


00:48:59.804 --> 00:49:02.305
- Want a drink?
- Um, no, I'm good.


00:49:03.407 --> 00:49:05.875
- Uh, I have something for you.
- What is it?


00:49:05.877 --> 00:49:07.476
It's the scene of crime video.


00:49:07.478 --> 00:49:09.111
The appeal's gonna be all
about the forensics,


00:49:09.113 --> 00:49:10.713
so you really need to see
that if you wanna know


00:49:10.715 --> 00:49:12.114
what's going on.


00:49:12.116 --> 00:49:15.751
- Joe was upset about earlier.
- Good.


00:49:15.753 --> 00:49:17.353
You know, he's good
at what he does.


00:49:17.355 --> 00:49:19.722
He gets ahold of stuff
no one else does and finds


00:49:19.724 --> 00:49:20.990
a way to tell a story.


00:49:20.992 --> 00:49:24.226
He's not as bad as he
likes to pretend to be.


00:49:24.228 --> 00:49:25.895
Are you sleeping with him?


00:49:27.865 --> 00:49:31.067
- Not tonight.
- Do you still sleep with him?


00:49:31.069 --> 00:49:32.301
Are you jealous?


00:50:00.931 --> 00:50:02.465
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:50:03.668 --> 00:50:05.901
Sorry, New York wants
me to change the article.


00:50:05.903 --> 00:50:07.436
They need it in two hours.


00:50:07.438 --> 00:50:09.138
Another fashion report?


00:50:09.140 --> 00:50:10.773
Jesus, lighten up.


00:50:11.541 --> 00:50:13.309
Does it never bother you?


00:50:13.311 --> 00:50:14.477
All this shit
you have to write?


00:50:14.479 --> 00:50:16.379
I'm not writing
a fashion report.


00:50:16.381 --> 00:50:18.347
I'm writing about a murder.
Somebody was killed.


00:50:18.349 --> 00:50:19.782
You trivialize it.


00:50:19.784 --> 00:50:21.550
People want to hear
about this story.


00:50:21.552 --> 00:50:24.320
It's not up to us to decide what
people should and shouldn't know.


00:50:24.322 --> 00:50:25.721
We just write what happened,
and then they


00:50:25.723 --> 00:50:27.656
decide whether they
want to read it or not.


00:50:27.658 --> 00:50:30.359
- That's not true. -Well, would it be
better if we didn't cover trials at all?


00:50:30.361 --> 00:50:32.194
People had no idea
what went on in court?


00:50:32.196 --> 00:50:35.297
People had no idea what went on
during a police investigation?


00:50:35.299 --> 00:50:36.899
That's what happens
in a police state.


00:50:36.901 --> 00:50:38.434
Then tell the truth,
don't make up the sexist...


00:50:38.436 --> 00:50:40.269
I do tell the truth,
you asshole.


00:50:41.405 --> 00:50:43.472
God, come back, Joe.


00:50:43.474 --> 00:50:46.008
At least he doesn't
lecture me after we've fucked.


00:50:47.344 --> 00:50:49.678
You know what,
you should watch this,


00:50:49.680 --> 00:50:51.614
before you get high
and mighty with everybody.


00:50:51.616 --> 00:50:53.482
That's the sad
and bitter truth.


00:52:45.695 --> 00:52:48.297
You are nurturing,
playful and easy-going.


00:52:48.299 --> 00:52:50.332
You often put others' needs
before your own,


00:52:50.334 --> 00:52:51.934
or your decisions are guided
by your feelings.


00:52:51.936 --> 00:52:54.170
- At heart, you're pragmatic and
self-possessed. -Oh, I love it.


00:52:54.172 --> 00:52:55.838
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you so much. Thank you.


00:52:55.840 --> 00:52:57.306
Thomas, how's the appeal going?


00:52:57.308 --> 00:52:59.441
- Yeah, quite right.


00:52:59.443 --> 00:53:01.043
No, no, no, no, no.
It's the right thing to do.


00:53:01.045 --> 00:53:03.045
I'll shut up. Give him a minute.
Go ahead, go ahead, go ahead.


00:53:03.047 --> 00:53:04.113
Slow.


00:53:04.115 --> 00:53:05.875
Do you think they're gonna win?


00:53:06.316 --> 00:53:07.917
No idea.


00:53:07.919 --> 00:53:09.585
Must be difficult
not knowing the ending.


00:53:09.587 --> 00:53:12.121
I don't think it matters
for our film.


00:53:12.123 --> 00:53:14.590
I imagine that the courts or the
police will find the truth.


00:53:14.592 --> 00:53:16.625
My idea is that it's
impossible to know.


00:53:16.627 --> 00:53:18.427
The trial is like an
episode of <i> X Factor.</i>


00:53:18.429 --> 00:53:19.895
If they like your face,
you win.


00:53:19.897 --> 00:53:21.931
- Oh, God. -The system
in Italy's different,


00:53:21.933 --> 00:53:23.966
which makes it easier
to see it's arbitrary.


00:53:23.968 --> 00:53:26.502
But in this case the evidence
is so contradictory,


00:53:26.504 --> 00:53:28.270
we'll never know what happened.


00:53:28.272 --> 00:53:29.638
If they killed her,
it doesn't make sense.


00:53:29.640 --> 00:53:31.640
If they didn't kill her,
it doesn't make sense either.


00:53:31.642 --> 00:53:34.476
So it boils down to,
do we want to see these people


00:53:34.478 --> 00:53:36.679
going to prison for 20 years?


00:53:38.481 --> 00:53:40.082
But in the film,
we're gonna have to decide,


00:53:40.084 --> 00:53:41.350
did they do it,
how did they do it,


00:53:41.352 --> 00:53:42.918
or how else are
we gonna tell the story?


00:53:42.920 --> 00:53:45.688
I don't think that's the story.


00:53:45.690 --> 00:53:50.059
The story is that there is no such
thing as real truth or justice.


00:53:50.061 --> 00:53:51.560
It's just a popularity contest.


00:53:51.562 --> 00:53:53.229
Well, that's not a film.


00:53:53.231 --> 00:53:54.730
I think it can be.


00:53:57.300 --> 00:53:58.901
Well, you're gonna have
to show the two girls,


00:53:58.903 --> 00:54:00.569
who they are,
their relationship.


00:54:00.571 --> 00:54:02.404
I mean, what happened that
night, why did it happen?


00:54:02.406 --> 00:54:04.240
All of that would be fake.


00:54:04.242 --> 00:54:06.942
It would be just my version of
what might have happened.


00:54:06.944 --> 00:54:09.612
It's more honest to say
I don't know what happened.


00:54:09.614 --> 00:54:13.882
It's like a detective story
in a world without God.


00:54:13.884 --> 00:54:15.484
Or a puzzle without a solution.


00:54:15.486 --> 00:54:18.053
Hmm. Would two people want to
do puzzles without solutions?


00:54:18.055 --> 00:54:19.421
Why not?


00:54:20.624 --> 00:54:23.459
It's more truthful than
all these easy answers.


00:54:25.128 --> 00:54:26.362
Well, it sounds
incredibly ambitious,


00:54:26.364 --> 00:54:27.630
which is what we wanted.


00:54:27.632 --> 00:54:31.033
If you want any help looking
at pages, the opening or...


00:54:31.035 --> 00:54:32.234
I'm happy to help.


00:54:32.236 --> 00:54:33.636
Thanks.


00:54:33.638 --> 00:54:34.837
- Great editor.


00:54:34.839 --> 00:54:36.372
- Seriously, no, honestly.
- Thanks very much.


00:54:36.374 --> 00:54:39.541
Top, top 25 under 25.


00:54:39.543 --> 00:54:40.643
What time is it?


00:54:40.645 --> 00:54:43.746
<i>It is four-something.</i>


00:54:43.748 --> 00:54:45.281
<i>What time is it there?</i>


00:54:45.283 --> 00:54:46.915
It's late, after midnight.


00:54:46.917 --> 00:54:49.251
<i>Oh, wow, that's pretty late.</i>


00:54:50.654 --> 00:54:52.087
<i>You must be really tired, huh?</i>


00:54:53.223 --> 00:54:54.290
I can't sleep.


00:54:56.092 --> 00:54:57.526
<i>Are you okay, Daddy?</i>


00:54:59.229 --> 00:55:00.629
Listen,


00:55:03.300 --> 00:55:04.780
I gotta call you tomorrow,
okay?


00:55:05.068 --> 00:55:06.869
<i>Okay. Bye.</i>


00:55:07.237 --> 00:55:08.604
Bye.


00:55:32.195 --> 00:55:35.731
<i>No sadness is greater than in
misery to rehearse memories of joy.</i>


00:55:47.678 --> 00:55:49.411
- Welcome back, Mr. Lang.
- Thank you.


00:55:50.080 --> 00:55:51.747
<i>How long are you staying for?</i>


00:55:51.749 --> 00:55:52.815
<i>Not sure.</i>


00:56:06.196 --> 00:56:08.130
No, it's nice.
It's definitely nice.


00:56:10.534 --> 00:56:13.135
Um, I've gotta go.
See you later.


00:56:13.137 --> 00:56:14.577
- Bye.
- Bye, guys.


00:56:15.171 --> 00:56:16.611
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:56:17.674 --> 00:56:19.375
Strange, seeing you
in the daylight.


00:56:19.377 --> 00:56:21.276
Why, do I look different?


00:56:21.278 --> 00:56:23.679
- Even more beautiful.
- Thank you.


00:56:23.681 --> 00:56:25.522
I like a bit of
old-fashioned courtesy.


00:56:30.387 --> 00:56:32.020
Hey, Edoardo.


00:56:32.288 --> 00:56:33.622
Hi.


00:56:35.759 --> 00:56:37.659
My friend Thomas is
looking for a place to stay.


00:56:37.661 --> 00:56:40.596
I told him I knew
someone who could help.


00:56:40.598 --> 00:56:41.830
Sit down.


00:56:47.804 --> 00:56:49.684
I'm too old for
a student accommodation.


00:56:50.206 --> 00:56:51.373
Well, I have lots of places,


00:56:51.375 --> 00:56:52.875
and the best addresses.


00:56:52.877 --> 00:56:54.176
Really?


00:56:54.178 --> 00:56:56.218
Did Simone tell you
something different?


00:56:56.880 --> 00:56:58.781
Be careful with her.


00:56:58.783 --> 00:57:01.703
If you believe everything she says,
you will never know the truth.


00:57:03.586 --> 00:57:05.087
Do you read my blog?


00:57:05.855 --> 00:57:07.222
No.


00:57:07.224 --> 00:57:10.859
You should. I say some very
kind things about you.


00:57:11.761 --> 00:57:14.263
- Didn't I, Melanie?
- Yeah.


00:57:14.265 --> 00:57:16.432
- Do you wanna drink?
- No, thank you.


00:57:20.703 --> 00:57:22.771
This was my uncle's house.


00:57:22.773 --> 00:57:24.239
He was a doctor.


00:57:32.348 --> 00:57:34.308
This is a perfect
place for writing.


00:57:34.951 --> 00:57:36.185
Full of atmosphere.


00:57:37.520 --> 00:57:38.787
I'll take it.


00:57:39.722 --> 00:57:40.956
How much?


00:57:40.958 --> 00:57:43.058
Money, we will talk later.


00:57:43.060 --> 00:57:45.961
First, I want you
to read my script.


00:57:45.963 --> 00:57:50.466
I have been watching your old
movies, and I like the naivete.


00:57:52.268 --> 00:57:55.637
I'm having a small
gathering of friends tonight.


00:57:55.639 --> 00:57:57.406
I'll come to collect you, okay?


00:58:27.904 --> 00:58:33.175
<i>"Then I saw a serpent with six
feet dart forth in front of a man."</i>


00:58:33.177 --> 00:58:36.478
<i>"With middle feet, it bound
him 'round the paunch,"</i>


00:58:36.480 --> 00:58:39.715
<i>- "and, with the forward ones,</i>
<i>his arms it seized.</i>"


00:58:46.189 --> 00:58:48.423
<i>"Already the two heads</i>
<i>had one become.</i>


00:59:58.061 --> 00:59:59.161
Come on, we are late.


01:00:00.096 --> 01:00:02.397
You know the way is hard.


01:00:02.399 --> 01:00:04.600
No one gets anywhere
by lying in bed.


01:00:05.468 --> 01:00:06.868
You have to work.


01:00:06.870 --> 01:00:08.671
Work even when
you don't know why.


01:00:09.238 --> 01:00:11.039
Where are we going?


01:00:11.041 --> 01:00:12.841
Where the thieves are.


01:00:13.142 --> 01:00:14.209
Oi.


01:00:16.679 --> 01:00:18.280
Thomas Lang.


01:00:37.767 --> 01:00:40.702
- Yeah? <i>Hey, Thomas.
Where are you?</i>


01:00:40.704 --> 01:00:42.337
I'm in... I'm in my flat.


01:00:52.315 --> 01:00:53.382
Hi.


01:00:53.384 --> 01:00:54.850
Hey.


01:00:54.852 --> 01:00:56.118
You good?


01:00:56.120 --> 01:00:57.319
Yeah.


01:01:00.556 --> 01:01:01.623
Where are we going?


01:01:01.625 --> 01:01:03.065
- To see Edoardo.
- Oh.


01:01:06.229 --> 01:01:09.331
I really think you should be
making a love story.


01:01:09.333 --> 01:01:11.733
All the best movies
are love stories.


01:01:11.735 --> 01:01:15.570
<i>Romeo and Juliet.</i>
<i>Casablanca. Annie Hall.</i>


01:01:15.572 --> 01:01:16.838
<i>Beauty and the Beast.</i>


01:01:18.908 --> 01:01:20.609
- Ciao.
- Hi.


01:01:25.248 --> 01:01:26.314
Hello, Thomas.


01:01:26.316 --> 01:01:27.416
Hey.


01:01:28.051 --> 01:01:29.151
What's the matter?


01:01:30.687 --> 01:01:32.988
Why you always seem so scared?


01:01:32.990 --> 01:01:34.990
What is it you're scared of?


01:01:34.992 --> 01:01:37.392
Maybe having to
make another movie.


01:01:37.394 --> 01:01:39.895
In case it's another failure.
Come on.


01:01:41.164 --> 01:01:43.098
Ignore him, it's all right.


01:01:48.771 --> 01:01:51.606
Don't worry, I know
the people who live here.


01:01:51.608 --> 01:01:53.909
- I own the house.
- I'll wait here.


01:01:54.510 --> 01:01:55.610
See you in a minute.


01:02:03.119 --> 01:02:06.855
The reason my script is good
is that I know what happened.


01:02:06.857 --> 01:02:11.059
Art has to provide the answer to
the questions that life asks.


01:02:11.061 --> 01:02:14.262
I know you don't agree
with me, but you are wrong.


01:02:14.264 --> 01:02:16.598
There is the truth,
and there is the rest.


01:02:17.734 --> 01:02:18.967
The killing happened here.


01:02:20.436 --> 01:02:21.503
I was watching there.


01:02:22.305 --> 01:02:23.872
I saw it with my own eyes.


01:02:23.874 --> 01:02:24.940
What happened?


01:02:27.009 --> 01:02:30.412
Joseph was in love with Elizabeth.
He wanted her.


01:02:31.414 --> 01:02:32.535
But she didn't want him.


01:02:34.117 --> 01:02:35.317
So he killed her.


01:02:36.753 --> 01:02:37.819
Like <i> Othello.</i>


01:02:40.790 --> 01:02:43.024
Like this.


01:02:51.634 --> 01:02:53.468
Sorry it's so noisy.


01:02:53.470 --> 01:02:55.303
Come with me.


01:02:55.305 --> 01:02:56.772
See you in a bit.


01:02:56.774 --> 01:02:58.039
See you.


01:03:05.982 --> 01:03:09.351
I have decided,
you can read my script.


01:03:10.686 --> 01:03:12.354
But you can't
take it away with you.


01:03:12.356 --> 01:03:15.023
I don't trust anybody
with my story.


01:03:15.025 --> 01:03:16.925
You have one hour, that's all.


01:04:29.732 --> 01:04:31.199
- Hi.
- Hey.


01:04:31.201 --> 01:04:32.901
- Can I come in?
- Sure.


01:04:34.871 --> 01:04:36.171
You look terrible.


01:04:36.173 --> 01:04:37.305
Do I?


01:04:42.678 --> 01:04:44.412
Where did you go last night?


01:04:44.414 --> 01:04:46.215
I was getting
worried about you.


01:04:46.716 --> 01:04:48.083
Edoardo freaked me out.


01:04:51.754 --> 01:04:52.988
It's so dark in here.


01:04:56.592 --> 01:04:57.859
No wonder you're depressed.


01:05:02.965 --> 01:05:04.032
That's better.


01:05:04.967 --> 01:05:06.967
I have something that
might cheer you up.


01:05:07.536 --> 01:05:08.703
You're gonna like it.


01:05:09.739 --> 01:05:11.406
<i>La Vita Nuova.</i>


01:05:12.275 --> 01:05:13.808
Thank you.


01:05:13.810 --> 01:05:16.645
Dante describes how he falls
in love with Beatrice.


01:05:16.647 --> 01:05:18.613
And then how she dies.


01:05:18.615 --> 01:05:20.715
For a moment, he toys with the
idea of loving someone else,


01:05:20.717 --> 01:05:23.885
but he'll never love
anyone like Beatrice.


01:05:24.954 --> 01:05:26.821
It's so romantic.


01:05:26.823 --> 01:05:30.358
All those circles of hell in The
Divine Comedy, it's boring.


01:05:30.360 --> 01:05:32.727
Everyone getting
punished for no reason?


01:05:32.729 --> 01:05:34.162
That is a book of love.


01:05:36.265 --> 01:05:38.667
Hopefully that will
make you happy.


01:05:38.669 --> 01:05:40.602
I'm late for class. I've gotta go.
Are you gonna be okay?


01:05:40.604 --> 01:05:42.237
- Mmm-hmm.
- Promise?


01:05:42.239 --> 01:05:43.838
- Yeah.
- Good.


01:05:45.408 --> 01:05:47.128
I just want you to be happy.


01:05:50.112 --> 01:05:51.179
I'll see you later.


01:05:52.014 --> 01:05:53.081
Bye.


01:06:30.052 --> 01:06:32.454
<i>"It was exactly</i>
<i>the ninth hour of the day</i>


01:06:32.456 --> 01:06:34.456
<i>"when she gave me</i>
<i>her sweet greeting.</i>


01:06:35.658 --> 01:06:38.693
<i>"I was filled with such</i>
<i>joy that I had to withdraw</i>


01:06:38.695 --> 01:06:42.230
<i>"from the sight of others and return
to the loneliness of my room."</i>


01:06:46.236 --> 01:06:47.602
<i>"As she walked down the street,</i>


01:06:47.604 --> 01:06:49.804
<i>"she turned her eyes</i>
<i>towards me,</i>


01:06:49.806 --> 01:06:52.240
<i>"where I stood in fear</i>
<i>and trembling."</i>


01:07:36.352 --> 01:07:38.232
- I need your help.
- With the film?


01:07:39.155 --> 01:07:40.321
With Edoardo.


01:07:40.323 --> 01:07:41.956
Maybe you should
steer clear of him.


01:07:41.958 --> 01:07:44.325
Maybe you were right. Maybe he
was involved in the killing.


01:07:44.327 --> 01:07:45.827
- Okay, stop.
- No, listen, listen, listen.


01:07:45.829 --> 01:07:47.362
I think he was there.
He took me to the house.


01:07:47.364 --> 01:07:48.596
He's got knives.
He saw the killing.


01:07:48.598 --> 01:07:50.131
He talks a bunch of shit,
he's messing with your head.


01:07:50.133 --> 01:07:51.399
No, I got to steal the knives.


01:07:51.401 --> 01:07:52.467
- I need you to help.
- No.


01:07:52.469 --> 01:07:55.603
I need you to get them to Rome,
to a lab, test them for DNA.


01:07:55.605 --> 01:07:56.971
- No. -I'll bring them
to you in the morning.


01:07:56.973 --> 01:07:58.339
Let go of me.


01:08:04.246 --> 01:08:05.613
Hello, Thomas.


01:08:05.615 --> 01:08:07.549
This is Thomas.
He's a director.


01:08:09.452 --> 01:08:11.453
I'm sorry I couldn't finish
your script last time.


01:08:11.455 --> 01:08:12.520
Yeah, why? You disappeared.


01:08:12.522 --> 01:08:13.822
I felt sick.


01:08:13.824 --> 01:08:15.523
Can I finish it?


01:08:16.492 --> 01:08:19.928
Okay.
You'll get another chance.


01:08:19.930 --> 01:08:22.363
But then you must tell me
that you want to make it.


01:08:33.375 --> 01:08:34.809
One hour, okay?


01:09:08.010 --> 01:09:09.077
Damn.


01:09:14.116 --> 01:09:15.183
Shit.


01:11:34.724 --> 01:11:35.957
Did you come to
my flat last night?


01:11:35.959 --> 01:11:37.025
Yeah, but you weren't there.


01:11:37.027 --> 01:11:38.747
Did you take the knives
from my bed?


01:11:39.194 --> 01:11:41.496
No. What... What knives?


01:11:41.498 --> 01:11:43.197
Thomas, Thomas!


01:11:43.699 --> 01:11:45.099
Thomas!


01:11:53.175 --> 01:11:54.642
What the fuck
are you doing here?


01:11:54.644 --> 01:11:57.145
I wanted to know
if you read my script.


01:11:57.147 --> 01:11:58.546
I didn't read your
fucking script.


01:11:58.548 --> 01:12:00.214
- Then you'll never know what happened.
- Get out of here.


01:12:00.216 --> 01:12:02.050
Get out of here!


01:12:02.052 --> 01:12:04.085
Have you been
looking for this, hmm?


01:12:04.087 --> 01:12:06.321
Did you think you had
stumbled on the truth?


01:12:07.022 --> 01:12:08.523
You're an idiot.


01:12:08.525 --> 01:12:12.026
These are film props. I
photographed them for my blog.


01:12:12.028 --> 01:12:14.729
And you should read it.
You wouldn't be so ignorant.


01:12:32.681 --> 01:12:34.615
- Where are the knives?
- Huh? What knife?


01:12:34.617 --> 01:12:36.484
Where are the real knives?


01:12:40.055 --> 01:12:41.522
Hey, hands off!


01:13:07.449 --> 01:13:09.717
You really have come off
the rails, haven't you?


01:13:13.389 --> 01:13:15.757
They're letting you go.
Let's get out of here.


01:13:18.260 --> 01:13:21.863
You're lucky. Edoardo's
not gonna press charges.


01:13:21.865 --> 01:13:23.825
Says you need a doctor,
not a prison cell.


01:13:26.402 --> 01:13:28.336
Looks like you hit him
pretty hard.


01:13:29.705 --> 01:13:30.905
Good.


01:13:32.408 --> 01:13:34.409
I'm going back
to Rome tomorrow.


01:13:34.411 --> 01:13:37.178
Stefano, Elizabeth's
boyfriend's willing to talk.


01:13:37.180 --> 01:13:38.513
It's his first interview.


01:13:39.214 --> 01:13:40.335
You should come with me.


01:13:40.649 --> 01:13:41.849
Yep.


01:13:41.851 --> 01:13:43.851
I have to get back to work.


01:13:43.853 --> 01:13:46.287
Get some rest
or something, okay?


01:13:46.289 --> 01:13:47.769
- Thank you.
- Yeah.


01:15:19.648 --> 01:15:22.049
<i>Have you written anything yet?
Yeah.</i>


01:15:22.051 --> 01:15:23.985
Really?


01:15:23.987 --> 01:15:25.620
Been thinking of
taking your advice.


01:15:25.622 --> 01:15:27.588
Making the film fictional.


01:15:27.590 --> 01:15:30.057
Setting it in Florence
as a tribute to Dante.


01:15:30.059 --> 01:15:32.026
Florence was the earthly
paradise he lost.


01:15:32.028 --> 01:15:35.830
Must be nice to have had an earthly
paradise, even if you lose it.


01:15:37.266 --> 01:15:38.566
Right?


01:15:40.736 --> 01:15:45.873
I don't wanna make a film about
fear or death or killing.


01:15:47.676 --> 01:15:49.517
I want to make
a film about love.


01:15:56.618 --> 01:15:58.853
<i>Yes?</i>


01:16:06.194 --> 01:16:08.996
I lived in the flat
below the girls.


01:16:08.998 --> 01:16:12.400
I met Elizabeth at the
beginning of the term.


01:16:12.402 --> 01:16:16.604
She came down in our flat
sometimes with Ana.


01:16:16.606 --> 01:16:20.007
We would hang out together,
smoke a little weed.


01:16:20.009 --> 01:16:23.077
Mmm. In court, it was
made very simple.


01:16:23.079 --> 01:16:27.982
That, um, Jessica was the bad girl
and Elizabeth was the good girl.


01:16:27.984 --> 01:16:29.684
She was just normal.


01:16:29.686 --> 01:16:32.253
She liked parties.
She liked having fun.


01:16:32.888 --> 01:16:34.922
She like making love.


01:16:35.824 --> 01:16:37.725
She was beautiful.


01:16:37.727 --> 01:16:41.729
I didn't know her for very long,
but I still think of her.


01:16:42.664 --> 01:16:44.365
I will always think of her.


01:17:04.686 --> 01:17:06.687
Ah, shit, I'm late.


01:17:06.689 --> 01:17:08.322
I'm gonna have to pick up
the kids on the way, okay?


01:17:08.324 --> 01:17:09.523
Sure.


01:17:20.268 --> 01:17:22.203
Hey, you guys,
I'm sorry I'm late.


01:17:22.205 --> 01:17:24.472
- Again?
- The traffic was really bad.


01:17:24.474 --> 01:17:27.408
- Andrew, Will. This is Thomas.
- Hey.


01:17:27.410 --> 01:17:29.310
- How was your day? Good?
- Good.


01:17:29.312 --> 01:17:31.178
Yeah? What did you do?


01:17:31.780 --> 01:17:33.180
Nothing much.


01:17:41.623 --> 01:17:43.958
- Your taxi's here.
- Thanks for looking after me.


01:17:44.559 --> 01:17:46.360
No problem.


01:17:46.362 --> 01:17:47.828
Bye.


01:17:49.931 --> 01:17:51.532
You talk to Katherine recently?


01:17:51.534 --> 01:17:52.600
No.


01:17:52.602 --> 01:17:55.436
You should.
Bea is yours and hers.


01:17:56.038 --> 01:17:57.705
That's how it is.


01:17:58.607 --> 01:18:00.047
- Bye.
- Bye.


01:18:01.276 --> 01:18:02.343
Take care.


01:18:10.886 --> 01:18:13.988
<i>Exterior. Siena. Night.</i>


01:18:13.990 --> 01:18:15.790
<i>The sounds of students partying</i>


01:18:15.792 --> 01:18:18.392
<i>drifts up from</i>
<i>the streets below.</i>


01:18:18.394 --> 01:18:21.429
<i>Elizabeth hangs out with</i>
<i>her boyfriend, Stefano.</i>


01:18:21.431 --> 01:18:24.632
<i>Sometimes Jessica</i>
<i>and Carlo are there.</i>


01:18:24.634 --> 01:18:27.968
<i>They smoke weed, drink beers,</i>
<i>go to parties.</i>


01:18:27.970 --> 01:18:29.670
<i>They're typical students.</i>


01:18:32.140 --> 01:18:34.875
<i>Elizabeth loves art,</i>
<i>music, literature.</i>


01:18:36.411 --> 01:18:39.580
<i>She visits the cathedral,</i>
<i>the galleries, the libraries.</i>


01:18:40.682 --> 01:18:43.484
<i>Siena is everything</i>
<i>she hoped it would be.</i>


01:18:43.486 --> 01:18:44.885
<i>She's happy.</i>


01:18:44.887 --> 01:18:47.321
<i>Looking forward</i>
<i>to the year ahead.</i>


01:19:04.372 --> 01:19:06.640
Back into the
belly of the beast.


01:19:06.642 --> 01:19:08.483
Yeah, let's try and avoid that.


01:19:09.244 --> 01:19:11.746
I booked you
a room in the hotel.


01:19:11.748 --> 01:19:14.014
- Keep you in the real world.
- Thanks.


01:19:19.020 --> 01:19:20.387
Heads up, verdict's at 8:00.


01:19:21.189 --> 01:19:23.390
- Hey.
- -Okay.


01:20:43.205 --> 01:20:46.340
We are thankful that Jessica's
nightmare is finally over,


01:20:47.075 --> 01:20:49.210
and we'd like to
thank the court


01:20:49.845 --> 01:20:51.946
for searching for the truth,


01:20:51.948 --> 01:20:55.082
<i>and for overturning</i>
<i>this conviction.</i>


01:21:21.509 --> 01:21:23.077
Justice has been done.


01:21:23.079 --> 01:21:25.579
They are right
to release Jessica.


01:21:25.581 --> 01:21:29.750
Uh, one young life had
been already tragically taken.


01:21:30.552 --> 01:21:32.052
Why take another two?


01:21:32.054 --> 01:21:33.621
Based on what?


01:21:33.623 --> 01:21:37.024
Assumption by the police and the
self-interest of the press.


01:21:38.059 --> 01:21:40.394
- Thank you.
- -Okay.


01:21:49.804 --> 01:21:54.174
Our daughter Elizabeth
has been completely forgotten.


01:21:54.176 --> 01:21:56.944
It's... It's very hard to
find any forgiveness.


01:21:58.513 --> 01:22:00.748
We know that four years
is a long time, but, um...


01:22:03.652 --> 01:22:05.219
Yeah, it's still very raw.


01:22:15.063 --> 01:22:16.530
Hey.


01:22:16.532 --> 01:22:18.132
<i>- Hi, Dad.</i>
- Hi.


01:22:18.867 --> 01:22:20.367
How are you?


01:22:20.369 --> 01:22:21.635
<i>Good.</i>


01:22:22.370 --> 01:22:23.437
<i>How are you?</i>


01:22:23.439 --> 01:22:24.538
I'm good.


01:22:25.807 --> 01:22:27.441
<i>Is the case over?</i>


01:22:27.909 --> 01:22:29.443
Yeah, it is.


01:22:30.979 --> 01:22:32.913
<i>What happened?</i>


01:22:32.915 --> 01:22:34.581
They say they were innocent.


01:22:35.283 --> 01:22:36.350
<i>That's good.</i>


01:22:36.851 --> 01:22:38.786
I suppose so.


01:22:38.788 --> 01:22:41.989
<i>So, does that mean you're</i>
<i>gonna be coming home soon?</i>


01:22:41.991 --> 01:22:43.424
I hope so.


01:22:44.526 --> 01:22:45.826
Is your mom there?


01:22:46.995 --> 01:22:48.062
<i>Yeah.</i>


01:22:48.730 --> 01:22:50.130
Can I talk to her?


01:22:51.700 --> 01:22:52.933
<i>I'll see.</i>


01:22:54.436 --> 01:22:55.502
<i>Mom?</i>


01:23:01.309 --> 01:23:03.077
<i>- Yes?</i>
- Hey.


01:23:03.079 --> 01:23:04.845
- Hi.
<i>- Hey.</i>


01:23:04.847 --> 01:23:07.114
I... I thought it would
be good if we talked.


01:23:08.283 --> 01:23:09.483
Try to talk.


01:23:09.918 --> 01:23:11.085
<i>Yeah.</i>


01:23:14.924 --> 01:23:18.492
<i>Let's, um... Let's do it</i>
<i>when you get back here,</i>


01:23:18.494 --> 01:23:21.295
<i>because, uh, I hate</i>
<i>speaking like this.</i>


01:23:21.297 --> 01:23:23.664
Okay. Yep.


01:23:24.632 --> 01:23:25.933
<i>Good.</i>


01:23:27.635 --> 01:23:29.269
<i>- Bye.</i>
- Bye, bye-bye.


01:23:29.938 --> 01:23:31.739
See...


01:23:56.364 --> 01:23:59.767
<i>Interior, church.</i>
<i>London. Day.</i>


01:23:59.769 --> 01:24:02.036
<i>Elizabeth's father reads</i>
<i>the funeral oration.</i>


01:24:03.705 --> 01:24:06.540
<i>It is taken from</i>
<i>Dante's</i> La Vita Nuova.


01:24:08.143 --> 01:24:11.245
<i>The power of my sighs</i>
<i>fills me with anguish.</i>


01:24:12.547 --> 01:24:14.948
Many times, while
contemplating death,


01:24:16.518 --> 01:24:20.721
it drains the color from my face, and
I begin to tremble from the pain.


01:24:23.892 --> 01:24:26.193
In weeping,
I call out to Elizabeth,


01:24:27.996 --> 01:24:29.930
"Can you really be dead?"


01:24:29.932 --> 01:24:32.299
And just calling to her
restores my soul.


01:24:34.436 --> 01:24:37.871
If anyone heard me,
they, too, would grieve.


01:24:37.873 --> 01:24:40.207
And what my life has been like
since she left this earth,


01:24:40.209 --> 01:24:42.209
there is no one that can tell.


01:24:45.713 --> 01:24:48.148
Elizabeth has ascended
into high heaven.


01:24:50.919 --> 01:24:54.955
<i>Into a place where</i>
<i>angels live in peace.</i>


01:25:00.195 --> 01:25:02.863
- Have a good trip.
- Yeah, we will. I'm driving.


01:25:02.865 --> 01:25:04.998
- Oh, okay.


01:25:06.734 --> 01:25:07.868
Hey.


01:25:07.870 --> 01:25:09.503
Hey.


01:25:09.505 --> 01:25:10.871
It's all over.


01:25:10.873 --> 01:25:13.407
No, there's bound
to be another appeal.


01:25:13.409 --> 01:25:15.809
This one's gonna run and run.
Thank God.


01:25:15.811 --> 01:25:19.813
Meanwhile, back to Rome, and
politicians with dirty hands. You?


01:25:20.882 --> 01:25:23.517
Going to Ravenna.
Sort of pilgrimage.


01:25:24.786 --> 01:25:25.953
Okay.


01:25:27.722 --> 01:25:29.056
Well, have fun.


01:25:33.528 --> 01:25:34.761
All right, I'm leaving.


01:25:37.365 --> 01:25:39.933
Oh, you're very
welcome to carry my bag.


01:25:39.935 --> 01:25:41.101
- Bye. Bye, baby.
- See ya.


01:25:41.103 --> 01:25:43.437
- You be careful.
- Yes, I will be very careful.


01:25:46.107 --> 01:25:47.441
Hello.


01:25:47.443 --> 01:25:48.642
Hi.


01:25:49.944 --> 01:25:51.278
Just getting the car.


01:25:51.280 --> 01:25:52.880
Cool.


01:25:55.049 --> 01:25:57.151
Look at those mountains.
Beautiful.


01:25:57.153 --> 01:25:59.073
I imagine you as a skier.
Do you go skiing?


01:25:59.454 --> 01:26:00.721
Yeah, I do.


01:26:00.723 --> 01:26:02.823
- I'm a snowboarder.
- Of course.


01:26:02.825 --> 01:26:04.424
Why of course?
What does that mean?


01:26:04.426 --> 01:26:05.692
You look like a snowboarder.


01:26:05.694 --> 01:26:07.027
I look like a snowboarder?


01:26:07.029 --> 01:26:08.662
Yeah.
Young, hip and cool.


01:26:08.664 --> 01:26:10.197
Really?


01:26:19.174 --> 01:26:21.608
Yeah. Jovanotti.


01:26:21.610 --> 01:26:23.477
- Do you know Jovanotti?
- No.


01:26:23.479 --> 01:26:25.812
Do you not?


01:27:01.049 --> 01:27:02.749
What a dump.


01:27:02.751 --> 01:27:04.751
No wonder Dante was
homesick for Tuscany.


01:27:07.555 --> 01:27:08.755
It's so flat.


01:27:11.192 --> 01:27:13.460
- Did you actually read it?
- Yeah.


01:27:15.763 --> 01:27:18.565
"O you who on the road
of love pass by,"


01:27:18.567 --> 01:27:21.802
"attend and see if any grief
there be as heavy as mine."


01:27:23.538 --> 01:27:25.372
There are two
different endings.


01:27:25.374 --> 01:27:27.474
The original version,
he ends up with a new wife.


01:27:28.876 --> 01:27:31.912
But later, he re-wrote it
to stay true to Beatrice.


01:27:31.914 --> 01:27:33.680
I prefer that ending.


01:27:33.682 --> 01:27:35.315
'Cause you're a teenager.


01:27:35.317 --> 01:27:37.651
I'm not a teenager,
I'm an adult.


01:27:37.653 --> 01:27:38.952
Twenty-one.


01:27:38.954 --> 01:27:40.687
But you behave like a child.


01:27:58.006 --> 01:28:00.641
It's incredible.
Dante's body is in there.


01:28:01.376 --> 01:28:02.476
So how old is it?


01:28:03.044 --> 01:28:04.678
Seven hundred years.


01:28:05.947 --> 01:28:09.483
Enough Dante. Enough death.
Let's go.


01:28:12.820 --> 01:28:14.521
- You want some?
- No, it's okay.


01:28:14.523 --> 01:28:17.891
Come on, you have to try it.
It's so good, please.


01:28:24.565 --> 01:28:28.001
It's funny, I used to go to
Dorset when I was younger.


01:28:28.003 --> 01:28:30.537
My mom and dad,
they always took us to a beach


01:28:30.539 --> 01:28:32.839
and made us walk for hours.


01:28:32.841 --> 01:28:35.542
I never wanted to go 'cause
it was so freezing and windy.


01:28:38.179 --> 01:28:40.113
They said it was good for us.


01:28:40.115 --> 01:28:43.417
Now I love it, but then,
I just wanted to stay home.


01:28:43.419 --> 01:28:45.285
Do you see them much?


01:28:45.287 --> 01:28:48.522
Yeah, when I go back to
London. They're crazy.


01:28:48.524 --> 01:28:50.824
They drove each other mad,
so they're separated now.


01:28:50.826 --> 01:28:53.327
- It's definitely better.
- Hmm.


01:28:53.329 --> 01:28:56.296
- What about yours?
- Still together.


01:28:57.031 --> 01:28:58.098
Amazing.


01:28:58.100 --> 01:28:59.580
- Yep.
- How long for?


01:29:01.069 --> 01:29:03.503
- Almost 50 years.
- No way.


01:29:03.505 --> 01:29:05.005
Yeah.


01:29:05.007 --> 01:29:06.106
One second, wait here.


01:29:09.544 --> 01:29:10.610
Ciao.


01:29:29.364 --> 01:29:30.731
- It's a present.
- No way.


01:29:30.733 --> 01:29:32.866
Why? Come on.


01:29:33.368 --> 01:29:34.634
Are you scared?


01:29:39.374 --> 01:29:40.774
Come on.


01:29:45.380 --> 01:29:46.780
Are you sure?


01:29:46.782 --> 01:29:48.315
What do you mean, am I sure?


01:29:50.051 --> 01:29:51.118
Oh...


01:29:52.754 --> 01:29:54.788
Don't be scared.


01:29:54.790 --> 01:29:56.757
It's so warm.


01:29:56.759 --> 01:29:58.558
- Is it?
- It's like, oh, my God.


01:30:03.831 --> 01:30:05.311
- Come on!
- Swim!


01:30:07.001 --> 01:30:08.668
Swim like a dolphin!


01:30:11.773 --> 01:30:14.374
Fuck you!


01:30:14.376 --> 01:30:16.610
You swim, you prick.


01:30:48.643 --> 01:30:49.976
Hi, Steve.


01:30:49.978 --> 01:30:52.279
Well, hello, I've been
calling you for days.


01:30:52.281 --> 01:30:54.815
- I'm in Italy.
<i>- Still?</i>


01:30:54.817 --> 01:30:57.250
Yeah. Flying home tomorrow.


01:30:57.252 --> 01:30:59.386
<i>Well, that's good,</i>
<i>'cause, um, we need to meet.</i>


01:30:59.388 --> 01:31:01.588
Not London. LA.


01:31:01.590 --> 01:31:05.892
Okay, uh, listen, mate, we've...
We've moved on.


01:31:05.894 --> 01:31:07.627
<i>Caroline insisted.</i>
<i>They want to make the film</i>


01:31:07.629 --> 01:31:10.797
<i>before it's too late and the heat's
gone out of the story, I'm sorry.</i>


01:31:10.799 --> 01:31:12.966
But listen, when you get
back to London, let's, uh,


01:31:12.968 --> 01:31:14.701
let's talk about
this face to face.


01:31:14.703 --> 01:31:17.003
I won't be back for a while.


01:31:17.005 --> 01:31:18.638
<i>But look, I am really sorry.</i>


01:31:20.575 --> 01:31:23.310
Don't need to be sorry.
Good luck with it.


01:31:23.711 --> 01:31:24.778
<i>Thanks, mate.</i>


01:31:24.780 --> 01:31:25.879
Bye.


01:31:25.881 --> 01:31:27.714
<i>Cheers, we'll speak soon.</i>


01:31:37.358 --> 01:31:38.692
Hi.


01:31:39.795 --> 01:31:41.161
How much is a single room?


01:31:41.163 --> 01:31:42.496
150 euros.


01:31:42.498 --> 01:31:43.964
And how much for a double?


01:31:43.966 --> 01:31:45.899
The same.
You pay for the room.


01:31:45.901 --> 01:31:47.661
It's fine. We'll just
get one room.


01:31:48.536 --> 01:31:50.570
It's all right, I trust you.


01:31:50.572 --> 01:31:52.706
Can I take your
credit card, please?


01:31:55.276 --> 01:31:57.410
Okay, check how many
cards you've got.


01:31:59.013 --> 01:32:00.080
That's fine.


01:32:03.651 --> 01:32:05.131
- Ready?
- Yeah.


01:32:07.622 --> 01:32:08.788
Wait a sec. Uh...


01:32:10.258 --> 01:32:11.892
On there. On there. On there.


01:32:12.927 --> 01:32:15.295
Oh, my God.


01:32:15.297 --> 01:32:16.563
Hold on.


01:32:17.465 --> 01:32:19.466
- No! Ugh!
- Yes!


01:32:19.468 --> 01:32:21.034
Spit!


01:32:25.072 --> 01:32:26.907
- What the fuck?
I mean, it was...


01:32:30.611 --> 01:32:32.145
Ah, stop it.


01:32:32.147 --> 01:32:34.147
- Spit!
- Ugh.


01:32:37.118 --> 01:32:38.385
One, two, three.


01:32:47.962 --> 01:32:49.029
- Spit.
- Spit.


01:32:49.031 --> 01:32:51.298
Yeah but I did
this one, it's mine.


01:32:51.300 --> 01:32:53.166
- No?
- Why did I choose this one?


01:32:53.168 --> 01:32:54.968
They're basically equal then.


01:34:05.106 --> 01:34:08.008
"Beatrice looked at me
and her eyes were full"


01:34:08.010 --> 01:34:13.947
"of sparks, of love, of such
divinity that, vanquished,"


01:34:13.949 --> 01:34:17.283
"my virtue ran away
and I was as if lost."


01:34:17.285 --> 01:34:19.352
"My eyes lowered."


01:34:30.431 --> 01:34:31.631
What do you miss about home?


01:34:32.633 --> 01:34:34.634
I miss my family, a lot.


01:34:34.636 --> 01:34:38.738
But, apart from that, um,


01:34:38.740 --> 01:34:43.009
bad weather,
and fish and chips,


01:34:43.011 --> 01:34:46.479
and pie and mash, and the tube,


01:34:49.016 --> 01:34:52.018
and I don't know what else.


01:34:55.923 --> 01:34:58.358
Yeah, it's beautiful.


01:34:58.360 --> 01:35:01.428
<i>The power of my sighs</i>
<i>fills me with anguish.</i>


01:35:02.697 --> 01:35:04.931
And weeping,
I call out to Elizabeth,


01:35:06.834 --> 01:35:08.435
"Can you really be dead?"


01:35:09.403 --> 01:35:12.005
<i>And just calling to her</i>
<i>restores my soul.</i>


01:35:15.409 --> 01:35:18.044
If anyone heard me,
they, too, would grieve.


01:35:20.648 --> 01:35:23.083
And what my life has been like
since she left this earth,


01:35:23.085 --> 01:35:24.718
there is no one that can tell.


01:35:28.489 --> 01:35:31.091
Elizabeth has ascended
into high heaven.


01:35:33.828 --> 01:35:37.997
Into a place where
angels live in peace.

